   233	
   234	### Gate B — PASS
   235	
   236	- B1: the precondition exactly formalizes the prompt's strings of `<` and `>`.
   237	  Empty strings are included.
   238	- B2: on this domain the supplied semantics' finite ASCII code sequences,
   239	  mathematical integers, Booleans, string iteration, and equality match the
   240	  relevant Python behavior.  No unsupported exceptions or external state are
   241	  involved.
   242	- B3: prefix nonnegativity rules out unmatched closing brackets; zero final
   243	  balance rules out unmatched opening brackets.  Their conjunction is the
   244	  requested bracketing property, and the execution-to-summary connection is
   245	  formally proved.
   246	- B4: the implementation agrees with all prompt examples and the independently
   247	  checked finite sample.
   248	
   249	### Gate C — PASS
   250	
   251	- C1: the only theorem-level trust boundary is the supplied `MPY` semantics
   252	  plus the K compiler, Haskell prover/backend, LLVM executor, and their integer
   253	  and Boolean hooks.  No proof-local unproved value or control primitive is
