   255	- C2: all claimed evidence has an existing artifact and exact command in
   256	  `prove.sh`; both negative probes expose their contrary concrete results.
   257	- C3: the positive result is reported as a partial-correctness theorem under
   258	  the supplied semantics.  Finite tests are identified as evidence rather than
   259	  a universal proof.
   260	
   261	## Trust ledger
   262	
   263	- Supplied `MPY` reference semantics: fixed theorem base; affects value,
   264	  binding, control, state, and modeled exceptions for both claims.  Evidence:
   265	  required LLVM build, eight concrete K assertions, and direct inspection of
